{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774970237,"nonce":"McGznldba5bVd2ko75UuH2ZRYF4=","title":"Add litellm proxy for overflow model remapping","message":"Add litellm proxy to the Docker container to enable model name remapping for overflow mode. Claude Code CLI validates model names client-side and rejects non-Anthropic model names, so we need a local proxy to intercept and remap.\n\n## Architecture\n\nWhen overflow mode is on:\n1. Container starts litellm proxy on localhost:4000 before the agent\n2. ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL points to http://localhost:4000\n3. Claude Code sends requests with standard Anthropic model names (e.g. claude-sonnet-4-5-20250514)\n4. litellm rewrites model name and routes to the configured provider (e.g. OpenRouter → MiniMax M2.7)\n\n## Implementation\n\n### 1. Dockerfile\n- Add `pip install litellm[proxy]` to the image\n\n### 2. litellm config template\nMount `litellm-config.yaml` into the container when overflow is active:\n```yaml\nmodel_list:\n  - model_name: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250514\n    litellm_params:\n      model: openrouter/minimax/minimax-m2.7\n      api_key: os.environ/OVERFLOW_API_KEY\n      api_base: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\n```\nThe config file lives in the project root (gitignored) or in `.nightshift/`. It's mounted read-only into the container.\n\n### 3. docker-entrypoint.sh\nIf overflow flag is detected (e.g. env var `OVERFLOW_ENABLED=1` or litellm config file exists at a known path):\n- Start `litellm --config /session/litellm-config.yaml --port 4000 \u0026`\n- Wait for proxy to be ready (curl localhost:4000/health)\n- Then proceed with normal agent startup\n\n### 4. host/docker_cmd.py\nWhen overflow is active:\n- Mount the litellm config file into the container\n- Set `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000` in container env\n- Pass `OVERFLOW_API_KEY` for litellm to read\n\n### 5. WORKFLOW.md overflow config simplifies to:\n```yaml\noverflow:\n  litellm_config: litellm-config.yaml\n  env:\n    OVERFLOW_API_KEY: $OVERFLOW_API_KEY\n    CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC: \"1\"\n    API_TIMEOUT_MS: \"3000000\"\n```\n\n### 6. .env\n```\nOVERFLOW_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...\n```\n\n## Benefits\n- Model remapping is config-only (litellm-config.yaml), no code changes to switch providers\n- Claude Code sees standard Anthropic model names, no validation issues\n- litellm supports 100+ providers out of the box\n- Proxy runs inside the container, no external infrastructure\n\n## Tradeoffs\n- Adds ~100MB to Docker image for litellm\n- ~2-3 second startup overhead for proxy\n- Extra process inside container\n\n## Scope\n- Dockerfile change (add litellm)\n- docker-entrypoint.sh change (conditional proxy startup)\n- host/docker_cmd.py change (mount config, set env)\n- Update overflow config parsing if litellm_config field added\n- Tests for the new launch path\n\nREQ: REQ-028 (overflow to alternate LLM provider)","files":null}]}